--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled third-party software
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Hindsight does not vendor third-party source. It downloads two upstream
binaries at build time (`make vendor`), verifies each against a digest pinned
in `vendor/checksums.txt`, and embeds them in the application bundle. Neither
is modified.

restic — https://github.com/restic/restic
  Copyright (c) 2014, Alexander Neumann <alexander@bumpern.de>
  BSD 2-Clause "Simplified" License.
  Provides the repository format: content-defined chunking, deduplication,
  encryption and integrity verification. Hindsight invents none of these.

rest-server — https://github.com/restic/rest-server
  Copyright (c) 2017, Alexander Neumann <alexander@bumpern.de>
  BSD 2-Clause "Simplified" License.
  Serves a repository over a loopback port in append-only mode so a server
  being backed up can write to it without being able to rewrite its history.

GRDB.swift — https://github.com/groue/GRDB.swift
  Copyright (c) 2015-2026 Gwendal Roué
  MIT License. Resolved as a Swift package dependency.

The full text of each licence travels with the upstream project. Run
`make vendor` to fetch the binaries; the script prints the versions and
digests it verified.
